last weekend war zone fans settled in  for part one of the world series of war  zone qualifiers everyone was looking  forward to a fierce and fair competition  to decide who advances to the finals  instead the whole thing was derailed by  widespread accusations of vpning stream  sniping and friends feeding kills to  each other let's untangle this whole  mess  vpns feeding kills and stream sniping we  really do have the holy trinity in  today's video if you enjoy hearing about  that kind of stuff when it happens then  make sure you're subscribed to the score  esports and if you enjoy the video at  the end of it make sure you leave us a  like on your way out the door appreciate  it all right before all this it had been  nine months since the last world series  of war zone event so as you might expect  fans were absolutely chomping at the bit  to see this event get started activision  have laid out a 300 000 prize pool for  teams competing in both europe and north  america for a total prize pool of 600  000  40 trios are competing in the open  qualifiers only 20 will make it through  to the finals but they then have the  chance to compete with 20 invited trios  to get their hands on that fat prize  money the scoring and rules for the  event are as follows and remember these  because they will be important later the  scoring is based on each squad's total  kills and placement in each map of play  players get a point for every kill and  additional points for teams based on  each of their squad's individual  placements then there are the  multipliers 16 to 40th place gets no  multipliers second to 15th get a 1.5  multiplier to their point first place a  whopping times two multiplier the  qualifiers are an open bracket anyone  could join it not just your usual scumps  and swags who get invites on paper this  seems like a great idea it increases the  chances of upsets dark horses and  underdog stories and who doesn't love  that but we wouldn't be doing this video  if things panned out like that because  unfortunately if there is a way for  players to manipulate a system some  often do you see warzone like a lot of  games has a matchmaking system you're  supposed to be mashed up against players  of equal rank and skill including in  this qualifier but not too far into the  tournament at all accusations began  flying around that some of the players  were using a form of vpn abuse called  geofencing youtuber the tactical brit  explained just how this  everything up what geofencing does is  prevents the game client from connecting  to various servers that call of duty has  available and in doing so prevents it  from being able to use skill based  matchmaking after about a minute and a  half to a minute and 15 seconds of  matchmaking call of duty automatically  gives up its skill based matchmaking  protocol allowing a player to get into a  game even if they're not necessarily  meant to be in that lobby so essentially  the game will deprioritize skill based  matchmaking after a certain amount of  time just to get a game going in this  tournament the belief was that higher  skilled players were able to get into  lower skilled lobbies through  geo-fencing and just clean up the  competition and because the tournament's  point system counts every kill the same  they racked up monstrous scores that  they probably wouldn't have got if  matchmaking was working as intended the  result was that these players were  getting closer to playing in the finals  against the best in the world with  scores that massively exaggerated how  good they actually are but all of this  wasn't even half the problem at the  tournament there were also accusations  that players were getting their friends  to join an opposing team in their  lobbies once they were in game the  friend would just die over and over  again to that player pushing them right  up the leaderboard one reddit post  shared some screenshots that show some  suspiciously high scores on one side  accompanied by some unbelievably bad  scores on the other one player getting  75 kills while their opponent died 34  times you get the picture a comment  suggested that the only realistic  explanation was that the second place  team was working with the first place  team to feed one of their players a huge  amount of kills get the win and the  multiplier that came with it and the  players being accused weren't total  randoms either one of the names in that  screenshot you just saw was mad lions  player javiks warzone streamer fifa kill  pointed this out on twitter and referred  to this as shameless he also got called  out as desperate by warzone streamer  porky9 and apparently in a later deleted  reply javik simply said that quote  everyone wants a spot the 75 kills that  the boosted player got might be enough  to get them into the final against some  of the best players in the world so you  can kind of see the problem here aside  from geo fencing and feeding kills a  third accusation flying around was that  streamers were being sniped in this  situation streamers were stuck between a  bit of a rock and a hard place on the  one hand they obviously want to stream  themselves playing one of the biggest  warzone events of the year but a number  of streamers felt they were being  targeted by players who would get into  their games on opposing teams ignore  everyone else and just hunt for that  streamer so to put it simply a lot of  warzone fans are unhappy with how this  tournament is panning out especially  because it has a knock-on effect the  invited trios are invited because  they're known to be absolute demons at  war zone there was excitement before  about seeing these pros face off against  hidden talents to battle their way  through the qualifier but that's going  to be tarnished now because a huge  shadow will be cast over the legitimacy  of the players who make it out of the  qualifier that sucks for those who don't  vpn abuse or feed kills to friends and  miss out on a spot because of that but  it also sucks for the ones who  legitimately qualify too because they're  gonna be doubted and of course it sucks  for the viewer too there's a good chance  that the invited trios are gonna  absolutely mop the floor with anyone who  didn't earn their spot in the finals  fairly this weekend we've got the second  part of the qualifiers for na and eu  we've had no word from activision so far  on what they're doing to address the  community's concerns here or to be  honest even acknowledge the existence of  them there's a chance we'll see more of  the same this weekend and if the drama  flares up again we'll be sure to let you  know  check out my excessive four liter water  bottle i got four liters i mean you're  supposed you know what's crazy you're  supposed to drink this in a day you say  it starts with 7 a.m finishes with 9 p.m  i think i get kidney failure if i tried  to drink that in a day
 

